  "question": {
    "text": "A line passing through the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> encloses an area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> with coordinate axes. The sum of intercepts made by the line on the <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> axis is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
